{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "scale-county-idle-adjust-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.57, step 7f. `scale-county-idle-adjust`: Total Energy (91) at running exhaust, extended idle and APU for the passenger car and the combination long-haul truck at Washtenaw County SINGLE scale, April and August 2020, both day types, hours 7 and 8, from the default database plus a county database that populates the six idle and hotelling ADJUSTMENT tables (`inputs/washtenaw-county-idle-adjust.esm`, built from moves.rs `setup-idle-adjust.sql`). MOVESOutput is 8,128 rows, 1,016 per time cell: running exhaust on road types 1 to 5 for every fuel MOVES adds to the two source types, extended idle (diesel and CNG), APU (diesel) and the APU's shore-power retag, process 93.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES is the two adjustment scripts no other database here reaches. AdjustTotalIdleFraction.sql replaces `totalIdleFraction` from `idleModelYearGrouping` and scales it by `idleMonthAdjust` and `idleDayAdjust` before off-network idle reads it (road type 1 of running exhaust); AdjustHotelling.sql rescales TAG's hotelling hours by `hotellingHoursPerDay`, `hotellingHourFraction`, `hotellingAgeFraction` and `hotellingMonthAdjust`, in that order, before extended idle and APU read them. Each table varies along every key it carries and leaves some key of the run without a row. Measured in pandas from the execution database before the port: the adjusted `totalIdleFraction` 20 of 20 at 2.2e-16, and the four-block replay of AdjustHotelling.sql on TAG's `IdleHoursByAgeHour` 984 of 984 `hotellingHours` rows at 9.6e-15 (PLAN.md §7.3.57).\n\n`n_outputRate` is bound to 1016, the rows per (county, month, hour-day) cell, recomputed as `rateSurvivorCount`.\n\n`db_movesoutput` is DECLARED AND CONSUMED BY NOTHING, as in every RunSpec here.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "fixture",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "single-county-domain",
      "road-type-axis",
      "off-network-idle",
      "idle-adjustment",
      "hotelling-adjustment"
    ]
  },
